# -*- mode:org; coding:utf-8 -*-
#+TITLE: alfe-dribble — the alfe half of the dribble feature
#+STATUS: TODO
#+PRIORITY: P3
#+TYPE: feature
#+DEPENDS: -
#+BRANCH: feature-alfe-dribble

* Context

=dribble.issue= specified the feature for *both* clautolisp and alfe
(with whatever backend CAD). The clautolisp half shipped in 1.5.11 and
was verified end-to-end on 2026-08-11 (clautolisp 1.8.28); that ticket
is now closed. This one carries the alfe half, which is not started.

Verified 2026-08-11: =grep -rn dribble --include='*.lisp'
autolisp-front-end/= matches **zero** files. Nothing exists yet, so
this is greenfield rather than a gap-filling exercise.

* Problem

An alfe session driving AutoCAD or BricsCAD produces exactly the kind
of interaction transcript a dribble is for — arguably more valuable
than the clautolisp one, since a CAD session is harder to reproduce.
Today there is no way to record it.

* Proposal

Mirror the clautolisp half, whose implementation is the reference:
=clautolisp/tools/clautolisp/source/dribble.lisp= (tee/echo Gray
streams, write-time interactor filtering, O/E/C tagging), driven by the
shared CLI spec in =clautolisp/autolisp-cli=, which already carries the
option slots — =cli-options-dribble= and
=cli-options-dribble-interactors= exist and their comment already reads
"clautolisp today, alfe planned". So the parser work may be close to
zero; the work is the alfe-side wiring.

From =dribble.issue=, the alfe-specific requirements:

- CLI: =--dribble=, =--dribble=FILE=, =--dribble-interactors=IS= on the
  alfe CLI.
- Default path: =${XDG_STATE_HOME}/alfe/dribbles/${BACKEND}/YYYYMMDDTHHMMSS.log=
  where =${BACKEND}= is =clautolisp=, =bricscad= or =autocad= — note
  the per-backend subdirectory, which the clautolisp path has no
  counterpart for.
- Header: =;; H: alfe $alfe_version clautolisp|bricscad|autocad $cad_version=
  — two version numbers, unlike clautolisp's one. Getting
  =$cad_version= means asking the live backend, so decide what the
  header says when the backend has not answered yet (or at all).
- Same interaction-block format: raw input, then =;; O:= / =;; E:= /
  =;; C:= lines, same line-interleaving rule.
- Append to an existing file.

* Open question

What counts as an "interactor" on the alfe side. The clautolisp filter
keys off =clautolisp.interactor:*interactor-stack*=, which an alfe
session driving a foreign CAD does not have in the same shape. Either
map alfe's own phases onto interactor names, or declare
=--dribble-interactors= clautolisp-only and record everything on the
alfe side. Worth settling before writing code — it is the one place
where the mirror is not mechanical.

* Acceptance criteria

- =alfe --dribble= against each available backend produces a file at
  the documented per-backend path with the two-version =;; H:= header.
- =--dribble=FILE= writes FILE; an existing file is appended to.
- O/E/C tagging and the interleaving rule match the clautolisp output
  byte for byte for an equivalent session.
- Documented in the alfe user manual and RELEASE_NOTES.org.
